 | Average Speed +0.0 km/h (133 vs 133 km/h) |\\n| **Sector 3** | 20.323s | 20.017s | +0.306s | **CARLOS SAINZ FASTER** | Average Speed +0.0 km/h (162 vs 162 km/h) |\\n| **Top Speed ($V_{max}$)** | 282 km/h | 281 km/h | +1 km/h | **Equal** | Peak straight-line aerodynamic efficiency |\\n| **Full Throttle %** | 32.0% | 32.9% | -0.9% | **Equal** | Total lap commitment at 100% accelerator pedal |\\n\\n**Sector-by-Sector Breakdown:**\\n- Sector 1: Carlos Sainz was quicker by 0.398s (19.530s vs 19.928s). Carlos Sainz reached higher top speed (269.0 km/h vs 267.0 km/h) with 33.3% full throttle duration (vs 28.6% for Charles Leclerc), maximizing top-end power.\\n- Sector 2: Carlos Sainz was quicker by 0.250s (35.266s vs 35.516s). Carlos Sainz maintained higher average sector speed (133.2 km/h vs 136.9 km/h) with cleaner throttle progression.\\n- Sector 3: Carlos Sainz was quicker by 0.306s (20.017s vs 20.323s). Carlos Sainz maintained higher average sector speed (162.1 km/h vs 163.2 km/h) with cleaner throttle progression.\\n\\nPerformance Summary: Carlos Sainz was the stronger performer across all three sectors (Sector 1, Sector 2, Sector 3).", "tyre_degradation": [{"lap": 1, "note": "START-LAP", "stint": 1, "status": "start_lap", "compound": "MEDIUM", "wear_pct": null, "pace_loss_s": null}, {"lap": 4, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 0, "pace_loss_s": 0}, {"lap": 7, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 0.4, "pace_loss_s": 0.01}, {"lap": 10, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 0.8, "pace_loss_s": 0.021}, {"lap": 13, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 1.3, "pace_loss_s": 0.032}, {"lap": 16, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 1.7, "pace_loss_s": 0.042}, {"lap": 19, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 2.1, "pace_loss_s": 0.052}, {"lap": 22, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 2.5, "pace_loss_s": 0.063}, {"lap": 25, "stint": 2, "compound": "HARD", "wear_pct": 2.9, "pace_loss_s": 0.073}, {"lap": 28, "stint": 2, "compo